  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two arrays, AAA and BBB, each containing NNN integers. You are allowed to perform the following operation as many times as you like (possibly, zero):\n\n\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), and swap AiA_iAi​ and BiB_iBi​.\nFind the maximum possible value that the expression\n\n(A1&amp;A2&amp;…&amp;AN)+(B1&amp;B2&amp;…&amp;BN)\\left(A_1 \\&amp; A_2 \\&amp; \\ldots \\&amp; A_N \\right) + \\left(B_1 \\&amp; B_2 \\&amp; \\ldots \\&amp; B_N \\right)(A1​&amp;A2​&amp;…&amp;AN​)+(B1​&amp;B2​&amp;…&amp;BN​)can take after performing the given operation several times.\n\nHere, &amp;\\&amp;&amp; denotes the bitwise AND operation.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN, the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the maximum possible value of the sum of bitwise ANDs of the arrays, after the swap operations.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai,Bi&lt;2300 \\le A_i, B_i \\lt 2^{30}0≤Ai​,Bi​&lt;230",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
